.TH AUTOCOMMIT 1 "October 2025" "autocommit 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
autocommit \- automated Git workflow toolkit with AI-powered commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ai_commit
[\fB\-m\fR \fImessage\fR]
[\fB\-\-pull\fR]
.br
.B autocommit
[\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIdirectory\fR]
[\fB\-\-commit\-message\fR \fImessage\fR]
[\fB\-\-pull\fR]
[\fB\-\-handle\-gitignore\fR]
[\fB\-\-remove\-ds\-store\fR]
[\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fIrepo\fR...]
[\fB\-\-only\fR \fIrepo\fR...]
[\fB\-\-no\-auto\-commit\fR]
.br
.B pull_repos
[\fB\-\-base\-dir\fR \fIdirectory\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fInumber\fR]
[\fB\-\-filter\-forks\fR]
[\fB\-\-only\-stars\fR \fInumber\fR]
[\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fIrepo\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B autocommit
is a Git automation toolkit that combines Go performance with Python elegance.
It provides three main commands for streamlining Git workflows:
.PP
.B ai_commit
generates conventional commit messages using a local LLM (Ollama), analyzes
git diffs to determine appropriate commit types, and automatically stages,
commits, and pushes changes.
.PP
.B autocommit
manages multiple Git repositories simultaneously, allowing bulk operations
across entire project directories with a beautiful terminal interface.
.PP
.B pull_repos
clones GitHub repositories in bulk using the GitHub CLI, with smart filtering
and detailed repository statistics.
.SH AI_COMMIT
.SS Description
The
.B ai_commit
command provides AI-powered Git commits with automatic message generation.
.SS Options
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message =\fImessage\fR
Specify a custom commit message. If set to "auto-commit" (default), an AI-generated
conventional commit message will be created based on the current changes.
.TP
.BR \-\-pull
Execute
.B git pull
before committing changes.
.SS Environment Variables
.TP
.B OLLAMA_MODEL
Specifies the Ollama model to use for commit message generation.
Default: "mistral"
.TP
.B OLLAMA_URL
URL of the Ollama API endpoint.
Default: "http://127.0.0.1:11434"
.SS Commit Type Detection
The tool automatically detects the appropriate commit type based on the diff:
.TP
.B feat
More lines added than deleted, indicating new features
.TP
.B fix
Diff contains "fix" or "bug" keywords
.TP
.B refactor
Diff contains "refactor" keyword or more deletions than additions
.TP
.B chore
Default fallback for maintenance tasks
.SS Examples
.PP
Generate AI commit message and push:
.RS
.B ai_commit
.RE
.PP
Use custom commit message:
.RS
.B ai_commit \-m "feat(auth): add OAuth2 support"
.RE
.PP
Pull before committing:
.RS
.B ai_commit \-\-pull
.RE
.SH AUTOCOMMIT
.SS Description
The
.B autocommit
command processes multiple Git repositories in a directory, applying the same
Git operations to all of them with a rich terminal interface.
.SS Options
.TP
.BR \-\-dir =\fIdirectory\fR
Base directory containing Git repositories.
Default: "~/Neoware"
.TP
.BR \-\-commit\-message =\fImessage\fR
Commit message to use for all repositories. If set to "auto-commit" (default),
AI-generated messages will be created for each repository.
Default: "auto-commit"
.TP
.BR \-\-pull
Pull changes from remote repositories before committing.
.TP
.BR \-\-handle\-gitignore
Ensure each repository's .gitignore file includes .DS_Store entries. Creates
or updates .gitignore files as needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-remove\-ds\-store
Remove all .DS_Store files from repositories using
.B git rm \-\-cached
and file deletion.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " \fIrepo\fR..."
List of repository directory names to exclude from processing.
.TP
.BR \-\-only " \fIrepo\fR..."
Process only the specified repositories. If empty, all repositories in the
directory will be processed.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-auto\-commit
Use manual git commands instead of invoking the
.B ai_commit
binary. This allows for more control but disables AI commit message generation.
.SS Features
.IP \(bu 2
Scans directory for Git repositories (directories containing .git)
.IP \(bu 2
Displays repository status with branch information
.IP \(bu 2
Shows file changes in tree format with status indicators
.IP \(bu 2
Provides real-time progress tracking
.IP \(bu 2
Rich terminal UI with colored output and icons
.IP \(bu 2
Detailed commit summaries with statistics
.SS Examples
.PP
Process all repositories in default directory:
.RS
.B autocommit
.RE
.PP
Process specific directory with pull:
.RS
.B autocommit \-\-dir ~/Projects \-\-pull
.RE
.PP
Clean up macOS files and update .gitignore:
.RS
.B autocommit \-\-remove\-ds\-store \-\-handle\-gitignore
.RE
.PP
Process only specific repositories:
.RS
.B autocommit \-\-only project1 project2 project3
.RE
.PP
Exclude repositories from processing:
.RS
.B autocommit \-\-exclude archive old\-code
.RE
.PP
Use manual git commands with custom message:
.RS
.B autocommit \-\-no\-auto\-commit \-\-commit\-message "Update all projects"
.RE
.SH PULL_REPOS
.SS Description
The
.B pull_repos
command clones GitHub repositories using the GitHub CLI (gh) with smart
filtering and beautiful progress visualization.
.SS Options
.TP
.BR \-\-base\-dir =\fIdirectory\fR
Target directory where repositories will be cloned.
Default: "~/Neoware"
.TP
.BR \-\-limit =\fInumber\fR
Maximum number of repositories to fetch from GitHub.
Default: 1000
.TP
.BR \-\-filter\-forks
Exclude forked repositories from the clone operation.
.TP
.BR \-\-only\-stars =\fInumber\fR
Only clone repositories with at least this many stars.
Default: 0 (no filter)
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " \fIrepo\fR..."
List of repository names (format: owner/repo) to exclude from cloning.
.SS Prerequisites
Requires the GitHub CLI (gh) to be installed and authenticated:
.RS
.B gh auth login
.RE
.SS Features
.IP \(bu 2
Fetches repository metadata from GitHub API
.IP \(bu 2
Displays repository details (privacy, fork status, stars, description)
.IP \(bu 2
Shows repository statistics after cloning (file count, size)
.IP \(bu 2
Skips already-cloned repositories
.IP \(bu 2
Rich progress visualization with panels and tables
.IP \(bu 2
Handles both public and private repositories
.SS Examples
.PP
Clone all repositories:
.RS
.B pull_repos
.RE
.PP
Clone to specific directory:
.RS
.B pull_repos \-\-base\-dir ~/GitHub
.RE
.PP
Clone only popular repositories without forks:
.RS
.B pull_repos \-\-only\-stars 10 \-\-filter\-forks
.RE
.PP
Clone first 50 repositories:
.RS
.B pull_repos \-\-limit 50
.RE
.PP
Exclude specific repositories:
.RS
.B pull_repos \-\-exclude user/old\-project user/archive
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/autocommit/
Configuration directory (if implemented in future versions)
.TP
.I .gitignore
Updated by
.B autocommit
when \-\-handle\-gitignore is used
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution
.TP
.B 1
General error (Git operation failed, repository not found, etc.)
